text @[Tomoya]
text ...
text A male student talked to me.
sound 4UA.aac
text @[Male Student]
text What are you doing here?
sound 4UB.aac
text @[Male Student]
text You've been here like, forever all by yourself.
sound 4UC.aac
text @[Male Student]
text Are you possessed by a ghost or something?
text There was nothing to say in return. Just like Fuko, I keep on standing there.
text She does not give up, so neither do I.
text @[Fuko]
text ...
text The girl standing before me never seems to change.
text Ever since the first time we met.
text How she keeps on carving even with an injured hand...
text Even with her clumsiness...
text Always single-mindedly, she keeps on working...
text ...You have...
text I gaze upon the tiny figure turned away from me.
text ...known everything from the beginning...
text ...and even about the ending waiting ahead.
text But maybe... that's exactly why she's been able to devote herself to her goal wholeheartedly and without hesitation.
text Yeah... She did say her voice wouldn't reach Kouko-san.
text Even if it did, it would eventually fall into oblivion, leaving nothing behind.
text That's right... In the end, this is the only thing she can do.
text Anything involving Fuko that has happened within this short month will turn into nothingness.
text And there is nothing we can do to change that.
text The unnatural happenings will be corrected by being removed from people's memory.
text Knowing that, she had to figure out...
text How she can leave behind her feelings...
text The feelings without form or even meaning...
text That's how she's been living all this time.
text Perhaps unconsciously, Fuko knew that she would never wake up...
text ...So she decided to appear in this school.
text All so that she could give her blessings to her sister's wedding...
text Even if she's not the person to give them directly...
text Even if she's to be forgotten...
text The back of the tiny figure before me...
text ...appears blurred for some reason.
